Confirming codex is right here — this is the one outstanding issue on this PR. `copy_session` already preserves `extension_data`, `recipe`, `user_recipe_values`, `project_id`, provider/model and `goose_mode` and replaces the conversation, so the `--edit --fork` path should just reuse it: fork via `copy_session`, then `replace_conversation` on the copy with the edited messages. That also collapses the duplicated `if edit && fork` / `else if edit` / `else if fork` branches into a single shape, e.g.:

```rust
if edit {
    if let Some(ref id) = session_id {
        let original = session_manager.get_session(id, true).await?;
        let conversation = original.conversation
            .ok_or_else(|| anyhow::anyhow!("session has no messages to edit"))?;
        let edited = crate::session::editor::edit_conversation(&conversation)?;
        let target_id = if fork {
            session_manager.copy_session(id, original.name).await?.id
        } else {
            id.clone()
        };
        session_manager.replace_conversation(&target_id, &edited).await?;
        session_id = Some(target_id);
    }
} else if fork {
    // unchanged
}
```

